          "final_text_tail": "essions). Parses the content via `_parse_block()`, an optional `pluralize [var]` block, then the **mandatory** `fallback` block (else `TemplateSyntaxError: expected 'fallback' block`), ending at `{% endctrans %}`. `trimmed` defaults to `environment.policies.get(\"ext.i18n.trimmed\", False)` and trims **every** block including the fallback.\n- **`_parse_block()`** (src/jinja2/ext.py:786): same parsing as `trans`'s (data + `{{ var }}` \u2192 `%(var)s`), breaking on `endctrans`/`fallback`/`pluralize`, raising `TemplateSyntaxError: unclosed conditional translation block` on EOF.\n- **`_trim_whitespace()`** (src/jinja2/ext.py:783): identical regex behavior as the standard tag.\n- **`_make_conditional_node()`** (src/jinja2/ext.py:825): builds an `If` node \u2014 true branch calls the environment's `gettext`/`ngettext` (newstyle \u2192 keyword args with `num_called_num` skip; oldstyle \u2192 `MarkSafeIfAutoescape` + `Mod` with a `Dict`), false branch renders the fallback constant with the same variable substitution, wrapped in `MarkSafeIfAutoescape` so escaping semantics match the standard `trans` output.\n\nVerified: all 830 existing tests pass, plus sanity checks covering true/false branches, both header styles, all three error cases (with the exact required messages), trimming (explicit, policy, `notrimmed`), pluralize (explicit/implicit var), newstyle gettext, autoescape, implicit/explicit/fallback-only variables, call-expression vars, and extension loading by string name. No existing tests were modified.",
